# §9 F multiple assignment / array decomposition / multiple return
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT ENTERS (docs/design/plano-secao9F-multi-assign.md):
#   - THE MULTIPLE-BINDING AST, in `src/parser/ast.tks`: `BindElem = BindName | BindSkip | BindRest`,
#     `MultiTargetKind = Parallel | ArrayDecomp`, and a new `MultiBind` `Statement` case; plus
#     `Return.values` and `Function.ret_types` (both empty on every existing node — fixpoint-inert).
#   - PARSER, in `src/parser/parse_stmt.tks` / `src/parser/parse_decl.tks`: `parse_multibind` (the two
#     lookaheads `var [` and `var NAME ,`, parallel / bracketed target lists with `_` and the ASCII `..`
#     skip-range, F-D1); `parse_multi_return_types` (a `( A, B, … )` signature, arity >= 2, `(A)` and
#     extern/bodyless rejected); and `return (e1, e2, …)` recognized only by a top-level comma inside a
#     parenthesized `return` value (`paren_has_top_comma`), so a grouped single `return (a + b)` is
#     unchanged and a bare `(a, b)` expression stays a parse error.
#   - CHECKER, in `src/checker/typer.tks` / `src/checker/collect.tks`:
#       * `type_multibind` DESUGARS multiple assignment and array decomposition to a FLAT sequence of
#         existing typed nodes (`TBinding` + a synthesized `if`/`panic` length guard), spliced into the
#         enclosing block and the two top-level statement sequencers via `TStmtSeq` — NO `TBlockStmt`
#         (the native backend does not lower it) and no new typed node, so codegen/LIR are untouched.
#         Parallel binds each value to a fresh position-unique temp first (parallel semantics); array
#         decomposition binds the source to a temp, emits the runtime length guard (exact without `..`,
#         minimum head+tail with `..`, ruling 5), then reads head elements at constant indices and tail
#         elements at `len - k`.
#       * `synthesize_mret_structs` is a pre-collect pass that lowers every multiple-return function to
#         an ORDINARY struct-returning one: it synthesizes one aggregate struct (`__mret…`, an
#         unspellable reserved stem) per distinct (namespace, return-type-list), rewrites the signature's
#         return type and every `return (…)` to that struct, and appends the declarations. Both backends
#         then emit the aggregate with their ordinary struct machinery — there is no tuple type in the
#         type system. A value-position guard (`type_is_mret_aggregate`) rejects binding a multiple-return
#         value to a single name (ruling 3), and `type_multibind_mret` destructures `var q, r = f(…)`
#         into aggregate field reads (`_mb._0`, `_mb._1`, …), `_` discarding its slot.
#
